data.content:
## .NET 10 OpenAPI Breaking Changes

The root cause is **Microsoft.OpenApi was upgraded from v1 to v2**, which targets **OpenAPI 3.1** (JSON Schema-based). Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `IOpenApiAny` removed
`Example` is now `JsonNode` (from `System.Text.Json.Nodes`), not `IOpenApiAny`.

```csharp
// OLD
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// NEW
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses a **type array** instead of a `nullable` keyword. `Schema.Type` is now a `JsonSchemaType` flags enum.

```csharp
// OLD
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// NEW — remove Null from the type flags
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

### 3. `ReferenceType` is now a struct, not an enum
The values are the same but accessed as static properties on a struct:

```csharp
// This likely still compiles, but if not:
// OLD: ReferenceType.SecurityScheme (enum)
// NEW: ReferenceType.SecurityScheme (static property on struct)
// Usage is the same — just be aware of the type change.
```

### Full fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");           // JsonNode
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;     // replaces Nullable
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of changes

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `using System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `new OpenApiString("1.0")` | `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` |
| `schema.Nullable = false` | `schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `ReferenceType` (enum) | `ReferenceType` (struct, same names) |
